Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.7
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    uses a statistically screened common-dictionary multi-task procedure.
    Candidate edges are discovered on the complete cell type and separately in
    every condition using the original Pando peak-to-gene, motif,
    peak-target-correlation and TF-target-correlation steps, and exact
    TF-peak-target triples are unioned into a broad candidate dictionary. A
    preliminary joint multi-task ridge fit is used to compute condition-wise
    ridge-Wald P values and BH-adjusted P values. Edges significant in at least
    one condition are unioned to form the actual common fit dictionary. The
    default adjusted-P threshold is 0.05 and remains user-configurable over the
    ordinary adjusted-P threshold domain (0, 1), without an additional
    condition-specific upper cap. All conditions are then refitted jointly on
    this same significant-union dictionary. TF-by-ATAC predictors use one common
    equal-condition within-condition RMS scale, matching the
    condition-specific intercepts and equal-condition loss while preventing
    between-condition mean shifts from changing the ridge penalty. Exported
    coefficients are back-transformed to the original TF-by-ATAC units for
    downstream projection. A positive ridge term makes the fitted system
    identifiable under collinearity or raw rank deficiency, and a symmetric
    fusion penalty shrinks condition coefficients toward one another without
    forcing equality. Each fitted condition receives equal total loss weight so
    large conditions do not dominate the joint coefficient solution. One
    target-specific lambda is selected for all conditions by
    condition-stratified cross-validation, using the one-standard-error rule by
    default. Raw design rank, condition-specific zero variance, regularized
    condition number and effective degrees of freedom remain available as
    diagnostics. The public target-condition rsq field uses
    dictionary-conditional out-of-fold R-squared, while in-sample R-squared is
    retained separately. In the final refit, a condition-specific edge is
    active for downstream projection only when its coefficient is estimable and
    its BH-adjusted ridge-Wald P value is below the configured threshold.
    Pairwise condition contrasts are calculated directly from the joint
    coefficient covariance rather than inferred from asymmetric significance
    calls. The coefficient and contrast P values remain approximate and
    conditional on data-dependent candidate discovery, significance screening,
    CV-selected lambda and fusion regularization. Standard infer_grn retains
    the original Gaussian GLM as its default method and additionally supports a
    single-task ridge method. Standard ridge is the K=1 special case of the same
    condition ridge solver, so the fusion term is exactly zero while the same CV
    lambda selection, within-task RMS predictor scaling, effective degrees of
    freedom and ridge-Wald diagnostics are retained. BiocParallel target pools
    can be supplied for both condition and standard ridge paths and are stopped
    after the corresponding fit when Pando started them. Independent cell-type
    jobs can also be dispatched through BiocParallel, and bundled reference
    datasets are installed as standalone RData files.
